I don't use fixed inventory letters, but I like to keep the beginning
of the alphabet somewhat orderly.  Otherwise, I'm not too picky about
what ends up where (foo-trices excepted, of course ... those get
bagged when not in use).

a - athame (or my musical instrument during the Castle Drawbridge
Concerto)
b - primary weapon
c - secondary weapon
d - tertiary weapon (if #two-weaponing and using a launcher too!)
e - quivered ammunition (but I don't obsess on where this ends up)

Spell letters, on the other hand, are a different matter.  I'm
somewhat OCD-ish on keeping them grouped by spell school and ordered
by spell level, with attack spells at the beginning.  Finger of Death
never winds up any later than 'f' in the alphabet, which cuts down on
accident potential.

